course: dictionary
lesson: 3497
title: Farmland: land used for farming
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Farmland is land used for farming: growing crops, like wheat, or keeping animals. You can work out much of the meaning from the parts you know, because farm and land are both in the word.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentences. «The prairies of North America are great farmlands for wheat.» The word wheat tells you what the land is used for. «Venice had little farmland but grew rich from trade.» Here little tells you there was not much land for farming, so the city had to earn its money another way.
explain: Watch for common phrases: acres of farmland, surrounded by farmland, good farmland. Test your meaning by swapping it in. «The village is surrounded by farmland» means the village is ringed by fields used for farming, so the swap makes sense.
fact: Farmland is land used for farming: growing crops or keeping animals.
fact: «Venice had little farmland but grew rich from trade between Europe and the eastern Mediterranean.»
fact: Geographers study how land is used, such as farmland, towns and forests.
fact: In science, farmland feeds people and changes the habitats where wild plants and animals live.
fact: «The prairies of North America have very rich black soil, and are now great farmlands for wheat.»
exercise: «Venice had little farmland but grew rich from trade.» What is farmland? | Water used by boats and ships | Dense forest where wild animals live | Streets and shops in a busy town | *Land used for growing crops or keeping animals
exercise: «The prairies of North America are great farmlands for wheat.» What is grown on these farmlands? | Ice | *Wheat | Coal | Sand
exercise: A town is surrounded by farmland. What does this tell you? | The town is made only of farms | *The fields around the town are used for farming | The town has no roads at all | The town is under the sea
test: «Venice had little farmland but grew rich from trade between Europe and the eastern Mediterranean.» Why did Venice grow rich even with little farmland? | Because it hunted zebras and wildebeest | *Because of trade between Europe and the eastern Mediterranean | Because it farmed wheat on the prairies | Because it had acres and acres of farmland
test: What does «good farmland» mean? | Land where crops grow well | Land that is under water | Land covered by deep snow all year | *Land used for farming that is good for growing crops
exam: Which sentence uses farmland correctly? | The farmland swam across the river | The steppes were farmland in the sky at night | Farmland is a loud noise made by trucks | *The farm sold its wheat and kept the rest of the acres of farmland for cattle
